# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal working documents — kept on disk, out of the public repo
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repository is public as a portfolio. What belongs here is the app and
# what someone needs to build it; planning notes, progress tracking, review
# transcripts and design screenshots are working artifacts, not source.
#
# These files still exist locally and are still written to — they are simply
# not published. Untracked 2026-08-15; `docs/` alone was 111 MB, and `_bmad/`
# (646 files of agent tooling unrelated to the app) had been committed by
# accident.
#
# ⚠️ Untracking does NOT unpublish: every one of these remains in the git
# history and can be recovered with `git log`. Removing them from history
# would mean a rewrite — new SHAs, a force-push to a public repo, and every
# SHA reference in JOURNAL.md and the merged PRs broken. Deliberately not done.
#
# docs/privacy.html is the exception that must STAY tracked: GitHub Pages
# serves it, and it is the privacy-policy URL declared to the App Store.

_bmad/
app-review-notes/
app-review-notes-2/
docs/screenshots/
docs/design-specs/
docs/design-review/
docs/reviews/
docs/known-gaps.md
docs/E2E_TEST_PLAN.md
docs/market-research.json
docs/AUTH_SETUP.md
docs/CI-SETUP.md
docs/handoff-swiftdata-test-crashes.md
